+# memory ranges (never trusted); if any fails, the original allocating
+# public path runs instead. All original validations run in the original
+# order before the first write. The arithmetic, its order, the zero-
+# increment compensation updates, the touch counter and the residual
+# maximum are exactly those of `_accumulate_single_process_sparse_validated`.
