+"""Construction, validation, bounded gathers and inventories of the
+resident-window voxel column (`WindowedVoxelColumnState`, CW-B3a).
+
+Authority recap (see the type's docstring): logical voxel `v` of cell `c`
+is the deep-store version below `base[c]`, the resident window inside
+`[base[c], base[c] + W)`, and exactly zero above. The version's own
+entries inside the window range are STALE after any exchange and are
+never read as mass: every overlay here writes the window over them and
+zeroes everything above, so nothing is double counted.
+
+Binding (root correction, boundary probe v2)
+--------------------------------------------
+A state binds to ONE version by `generation == version.version_id` AND
+`manifest_digest == version.manifest_digest`. Sibling versions (two
+journals applied to the same parent) share a `version_id` but never a
+manifest digest, so the digest is what refuses a swapped sibling whose
+deep inventory differs from the metadata the state carries. The cheap
+validator checks both before any fast operation; the trusted-boundary
+validator additionally streams the version and requires the metadata
+bitwise.
+
+Reductions and exactness (design corrected report section 6.2)
+---------------------------------------------------------------
+* STORED values (window entries, deep chunk entries) are exact: a
+  windowed column built from a dense one reproduces it byte for byte
+  through `gather_full_columns` / `windowed_to_dense`.
+* Every DERIVED reduction defined by this module is an EXPLICIT ordered
+  fold of elementwise IEEE additions, so it is the same declared
+  arithmetic on NumPy and CuPy (root item 4): `deep_by_class_kg` is the
+  sequential prefix `((v0 + v1) + v2) + ...` over voxels `[0, base)`
+  (`sequential_prefix_by_class`); `deep_room_kg` the same fold of
+  `max(capacity - voxel_total, 0)`; `deep_total_kg` and every class total
+  here the sequential class fold `((c0 + c1) + c2) + ...`
+  (`sequential_class_fold`); `column_mass_by_class_kg` extends the deep
+  prefix in slot order through the `W` window slots. The ONE library
+  reduction used is the per-voxel class total `sum(axis=-1)` inside the
+  dense MAPLE validator and in `voxel_totals_for_window`, exactly the
+  dense convention. Whether the explicit fold equals NumPy's
+  `mass_kg.sum(axis=-2)` bitwise is NOT claimed: the probe
+  (`probe_sequential_axis_reduction`, `tests/conservative_window/
+  test_reduction_order_probe.py`) records it per layout and NumPy
+  version, and the differential tests compare derived reductions within
+  the existing `summation_error_bound_kg(n_voxels + 1, capacity)`
+  contract, asserting bitwise only where the probe passed for that
+  layout. No new fitted tolerance is introduced.
+* Domain inventories reuse the existing MAPLE staged fold
+  (`maple.aeolian.flux.step._staged_class_totals_kg`) on each resident
+  part, with the active layer added separately (bounded by MAPLE's own
+  policy; cross-backend agreement of that fold is MAPLE's existing
+  contract, not changed here).
+
+Residency and memory
+--------------------
+Construction is HOST-side and streamed in row bands / chunks; it never
+holds a second full dense array (the caller's own dense input, in
+`windowed_column_from_dense`, is read in bands and never copied whole).
+The window and metadata may then be moved with `to_device_tree`, which
+passes the opaque deep-store handle through untouched. The cheap
+validator reads one batch of flags from the window's own namespace; the
+full validator streams the deep store on the host and converts the window
+one chunk-slice at a time through the counted `to_host`.
+
+The class-fold loops run over `n_classes` and the prefix loops over
+`n_voxels`: both are construction/validation/diagnostic paths of this
+storage slice, not the per-step exchange hot path (CW-B3b), and they are
+vectorised over every cell of the band or chunk being processed.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import dataclasses
+from pathlib import Path
+from typing import Any
+
+import numpy as np
+
+from maple.core.backend import (
+    MapleArray,
+    array_namespace,
+    finite_flag,
+    is_array,
+    namespace_name,
+    negative_flag,
+    read_flags,
+    to_host,
+    to_int,
+    true_flag,
+)
